    "created_at": "2017-05-03T20:42:38Z",
    "updated_at": "2017-05-03T20:42:38Z",
    "body": "Besides some of the use cases described in https://github.com/w3c/performance-timeline/issues/13#issuecomment-111152115, we're also having a need for a Fetch Observer when trying to develop a Time-To-Interactive metric that's based on signals like LongTasks, FPS, and networking activity.    \r\n\r\nWe'd like to know when networking activity is below some level (i.e. n resources outstanding), and there's no way to do this today in a complete and performant way.",
